## Why This Is Asked

This tests ability to design end-to-end, multi-tenant privacy-conscious tests for streaming data, including isolation, schema evolution, and canary risk.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenancy isolation
- Data privacy and retention
- Schema evolution and backward compatibility
- Streaming backpressure and performance
- Canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: simple data leakage check
function checkIsolation(records) {
  const seenTenants = new Set();
  for (const r of records) {
    if (seenTenants.has(r.tenantId)) return false;
    seenTenants.add(r.tenantId);
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you generate tenant-scoped synthetic data with privacy constraints?
- What instrumentation would you add to verify no cross-tenant leakage under burst load?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for data pipelines in lakehouse environments require validating schema evolution, data quality, and time-travel correctness under high throughput.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end test harness for streaming ingestion
- Schema evolution handling and back/forward compatibility
- Idempotent upserts and deduplication keys
- Time-travel validation and backfill scenarios
- Canary rollout and rollback criteria
- Latency and throughput budgets in a Snowflake context

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-data generator for evolving schema
function genEvent(version){
  const base={id: crypto.randomUUID(), ts: Date.now(), v: version}
  if(version>=2) base.meta = {src: 'prod'};
  if(version>=3) base.payload = {val: Math.random()};
  return base;
}
```

